HOW TO READ THE TWO COLUMNS
  'mean' buys and sells at each minute's close -- optimistic, because a
  market order pays the offer and minute bars carry no quotes at all.
  'worst-case mean' buys at the entry minute's HIGH and sells at the exit
  minute's LOW, which is the worst pair of prices actually printed. Any
  real fill sits between them. A result that only survives the first
  column is a result about the spread, not about the filing.

